      "reason": "Retain p150 and p192 together, with a precise evidence scope. The actual p150 description explicitly permits splitting into previously learned shapes and adding or subtracting their areas; its second criterion covers combining the pieces. The triangle/rectangle criterion is one demonstrated partition skill, not an explicit exclusion of other learned shapes. Circle-area knowledge is separately represented by p192. Thus the semicircle composition is supported by the existing descriptions without broadening either node or creating one. This question supplies evidence for area combination and circle area, not direct evidence of triangle/rectangle partition proficiency. With AC=2u, CE=3u, semicircle areas scale as 4,9,25; shaded and unshaded totals are 25-4+9=30 and 25+4-9=20, giving source C, 3:2. The bound figure confirms those signs.",
